# Normalise line endings.
#
# Two machines (laptop + Dell) check out the same files. Without this, Git
# converts CRLF/LF differently per machine and every file looks modified on the
# other one — `git diff` reported 436 changed lines in publish.py when the real
# answer was zero. Worse, publish.py would commit and push that phantom churn
# every night forever.
#
# text=auto eol=lf: store LF in the repo, and since these are all tools that
# handle LF fine on Windows (Python, git bash, browsers), check out LF too.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must keep CRLF or cmd.exe can mis-parse them.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
